issues.issue:
opd-17 is undersized and unsafe as one increment. Readmitting onto the same patient row breaks single-stay assumptions across the codebase:
- admissions has no uniqueness or index on (patient_id, status='active'), so a double active admission is possible;
- patient_profiles has patient_id as PRIMARY KEY, and admit_patient INSERTs it;
- each admission creates a new case_room channel and sage_room_memory row;
- discharge_summaries carries no admission_id;
- the /vigil/discharged list LEFT JOINs discharge_summaries, so a twice-discharged patient appears twice;
- NABH inpatient-days and the shadow scorecard derive stays from patients.admission_date plus MAX(discharged_at).
The dev DB has zero patients with more than one admission, so none of this is exercised anywhere.

increments.description:
New registration_service.py, patient_matching.py (normalizers) and registration_routes.py, registered in main.py.
- Register in one immediate transaction:
  - status 'registered', no portal login, no allergy field;
  - UHID in hospital mode (site pattern plus uniqueness) or orb mode (billing_masters.allocate_series_number with the caller's handle, no yearly reset, Verhoeff digit);
  - DOB or stated age with age_recorded_on;
  - patient_demographics row;
  - ABHA placeholder through a new abdm_service.record_abha_on(db);
  - audit in the same transaction under a new fail-closed 'patient_identity' category.
- Search returns masked minimal fields (UHID, name, sex, age, phone last 4, last visit, status), minimum 3 characters, limit 20, phi_access audited.
- Read registration record.
- Correct demographics: reason and row_version required; UHID correction admin-only; appends patient_identity_changes.
- New require_registration_access guard, entered in the drift-guard exempt set with its reason.
- Classify demographics and changes under the clinical_record retention policy.

frontdesk_service and routes:
- call (alias of start), skip, recall, assign-to-me;
- PATCH priority/room;
- ordering by priority then token.
New /api/opd/my-queue. New OpdPanel.tsx tab ('clinical' group, doctor and clinician only): call next, skip, recall, take unassigned. shellConfig: CLINICAL_MODULE_IDS becomes ['dietary','opd'], with the pinning test updated and its reason. A content-free 'opd:queue_changed' {department} nudge is emitted by importing sio (realtime.py itself is not edited); clients refetch over scoped REST. The front desk queue shows priority, room and skipped.

Migration M51: opd_consultations plus append-only opd_consultation_addenda. New opd_service.py:
- draft and save with row_version;
- sign: immutable afterwards, written in-transaction with its audit;
- addenda and history;
- ICD-10 validated through terminology_service, with an optional problem_list add;
- OPD vitals kept in vitals_json with measured_at; never written to vitals or risk_scores and never scored.
Routes under /api/opd: consultation GET/PUT, sign, addenda, complete-with-disposition (keeps the existing charge logic), patients/{patient_id}/consultations behind require_patient_access. patient_timeline_service shows OPD visits and signed consultations.

Migration M54: in-transaction rebuild of appointments (not an FK parent) adding checked_in and no_show statuses, the doctor, session and attendance columns, and a partial unique index on live doctor slots (pre-checked for existing clashes). appointments_routes:
- doctor and slot booking, double-book returns 409;
- reschedule (new row linked to the old);
- check-in creates the OPD visit with appointment_id and a token;
- no-show: manual, or computed at session end on read (no background loop);
- fixes the unscoped cancel and complete routes and the date.today() in /mine.
forecast get_appointments returns the doctor. Front Desk 'Appointments' day view; AppointmentsPanel shows the doctor. Patient portal requests stay as they are.

admission_service.admit_existing_patient refactors admit_patient's inserts into shared helpers so one transaction:
- moves status from 'registered' or 'discharged' to 'admitted' with no new patient or MRN;
- creates a Bridge login only if none exists;
- links admissions.opd_visit_id and the visit (disposition 'admitted');
- carries the provisional diagnosis and complaint;
- keeps charted allergies;
- writes a clinical_access audit in-transaction (scope moves to the ward).
POST /api/admissions/admit-existing. A duplicate MRN on /admit becomes 409 naming no patient. AdmitPatientModal gets an existing-patient mode: identity fixed, demographics read-only, OPD vitals and OPD medicines shown for reference only with their times. OpdPanel 'Advise admission'. Uses the adt-1 bed picker if it has landed. Shared with the Ward Record 'returning patient reopens the same record' item.

GET /api/frontdesk/mis/daily returns aggregates only for one hospital-local day:
- new vs returning registrations;
- visits by clinic and doctor;
- median and longest wait, LWBS;
- no-shows (when opd-16 is in), OPD-to-IP conversions.
Front Desk 'Day summary' view with CSV export.

risks:
Defects found while mapping, outside any running session:
- appointment cancel and complete are not ward-scoped (appointments_routes.py:476-598);
- /api/appointments/mine uses the server's date.today() (:423);
- the ghost POST /api/vigil/patients is still live and used by soak_test.py;
- front-desk OPD audits are written after commit in a fail-soft category.
The first three are fixed inside opd-16 and opd-1, and are worth a separate quick fix before then.

